documentation.registry-registry-components-pages:
# Page sections

Page-building sections use the existing `page-` filename and item prefix.

```structures-rules
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "page-prefix",
      "match": "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}",
      "name": "page-[a-z0-9-]+\\.(?:ts|tsx|mts|cts)"
    }
  ]
}
```

documentation.registry-registry-components:
# Portable components

Direct files render reusable UI. The five child directories separate layouts, page sections, plugins, connectors and nonvisual utilities. Published import paths remain stable.

## Module naming rules

Use kebab-case basenames and folder names. Preserve dot suffixes such as `.server.ts`, declarations and existing `index.ts` entry points. Placement follows CONTRIBUTING.md and the distribution checks in tests/registry-structure.test.mjs.

```structures-rules
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "module-names",
      "match": "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}",
      "case": "kebab-case"
    },
    {
      "id": "folder-names",
      "match": "**",
      "kind": "folder",
      "case": "kebab-case"
    },
    {
      "id": "portable-source-placement",
      "match": "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}",
      "path": "(?:[^/]+\\.(?:ts|tsx|mts|cts)|(?:connectors|layouts|pages|plugins|utils)/.+)"
    }
  ]
}
```

documentation.registry-src:
# Showroom application

TanStack Start application, kept separate from portable registry source. Existing aliases in tsconfig.json resolve @/components into registry/ and other @/ imports into src/.

## Module naming rules

Use kebab-case TypeScript basenames outside routes. Keep existing `.server.ts`, `.d.ts` and other role suffixes. Preserve TanStack route filenames and generated routeTree.gen.ts.

```structures-rules
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "showroom-module-names",
      "match": "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}",
      "exclude": [
        "routes/**",
        "routeTree.gen.ts"
      ],
      "case": "kebab-case"
    }
  ]
}
```

documentation.registry-tests:
# Tests

Node unit tests, browser journeys, integration suites and their fixtures. Keep test helpers with their suite, such as tests/agents/mcp-client.mjs. Integration containers and migrations remain within their existing test directories.

## Module naming rules

Use kebab-case basenames. Preserve `.test.mjs`, `.browser.mjs`, `.integration.mjs`, `.fixture.tsx` and existing fixture/helper extensions.

```structures-rules
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "test-module-names",
      "match": "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts,mjs,cjs}",
      "case": "kebab-case"
    }
  ]
}
```

documentation.registry-scripts:
# Repository scripts

Local development and maintenance entry points, including the disposable demo-mcp.mjs server. These are not installed registry items.

## Module naming rules

Use kebab-case source basenames, preserving the existing language and module extension.

```structures-rules
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "script-module-names",
      "match": "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts,mjs,cjs,js}",
      "case": "kebab-case"
    }
  ]
}
```
